# No comments

Hate comments. No narration. No section banners. No commented-out corpses. No
workaround sermons. No restating next line in English. Delete on touch.

Code obvious from names, types, structure, tests. Need paragraph to pass review?
Code broken. Reshape. No prose alibi.

Only these keep:

- Legal or license headers.
- Non-obvious behavior forced by external dependency, platform, vendor,
  protocol, or toolchain we cannot change. Surprise in our code = bug: rename,
  extract, type, or rearchitect. Cannot fix this change? Mark exact symbol
  `MUST KILL`.
- Tool directives that change codegen or formatting (`fmt`/`nolint`/`nixfmt`
  ignores, and like). Lint or type suppressions keep only when rule faulty,
  pedantic, or style-only. Rule catch real bugs or protect correctness/safety?
  Kill suppression. Mark guilty symbol `MUST KILL`.
- Doc comments that define public API contract (exported options, module
  interfaces, library surfaces). Not restating signature.
- Issue, ADR, or RFC links that explain constraint code cannot express.

List = only leash. Doubt? Comment dies.

`IMPORTANT`, `do not remove`, `too risky`, `fine for now`, long justifications =
scent not proof. Read nearby code. Only foreign keep-list gotcha proven true on
live path stays. Never polish meat into shorter alibi.

When edit: delete dead comments in scope. No narration. No comment-out — delete;
git remembers. Out-of-scope reshape? Report `MUST KILL` one line each.
